The match ended, and we were very tired.
Kasper, Sara, and I played badminton for almost two hours.
We walked over to a bench.
We sat down together.
I opened my bag and found my water bottle.
We just drank cold water for a long time.
"That was a tough match," Kasper said.
Sara smiled and looked at me.
"You came to Denmark in January, right?" she asked.
"Yes, I traveled from Mexico in the middle of January," I answered.
Kasper put his racket on the bench.
"How were your first days in the country?" he asked.
I thought back to my first week.
Everything was new and very different back then.
I didn't know the city at all.
"It was very cold," I began.
Kasper and Sara laughed loudly.
"The Danish winter is always cold," Sara said.
Kasper asked me.
"What happened on your very first day?"
